// src/kernel/boot/witness/r56_meta.pdx — R56.M3-006 (#1795)
//
// Dormant composite scaffold for the VFS-metadata syscall block
// (mkdir/rmdir/stat/getdents/unlink/rename, sysnos 77..82) landed
// by the R56.M3-002..005 wave (#1791..#1794).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What this witness proves
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//   (A) The `r56_meta_witness` symbol links into build/kernel.elf
//       and is reachable as a `call r56_meta_witness` target from
//       GDB or from a future kernel_main wire-up.
//
//   (B) Nothing else. The body is a symbol-existence scaffold that
//       returns 77 (SKIP sentinel) without touching any of the six
//       sys_*_body entrypoints. Fingerprint emission for each body
//       is already covered per-primitive by the R56.M3-002..005
//       individual goldens (see tests/r56/expected-r56-{mkdir-rmdir,
//       stat,getdents,unlink-rename}.txt) — the R56.M3-006 golden at
//       tests/r56/expected-r56-meta.txt aggregates the composite
//       6-line sequence for the future ring-3 harness to match.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Why the body is deferred (not "future work in general")
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Every sys_*_body in the R56.M3 wave (sys_mkdir.pdx, sys_stat.pdx,
// sys_getdents.pdx, sys_rmdir.pdx, sys_unlink.pdx, sys_rename.pdx)
// walks its caller-supplied path via `user_read_str_via_walk` on a
// user virtual address. That walker resolves the VA against the
// current task's page tables, so a kernel-side call site handing
// it a .bss scratch buffer either misses the mapping (walker returns
// 0 -> EFAULT) or, worse, faults on a kernel-only page. Making the
// composite witness invoke the six bodies from ring 0 therefore
// requires one of:
//
//   (i)  Forging a synthetic user aspace (dedicated pml4 + user-VA
//        mapping of the scratch pages) around the call sequence,
//        restoring cr3 on exit; OR
//   (ii) Launching a real ring-3 harness that exercises the six
//        syscalls via `syscall` / `int 0x80` from userspace, which
//        composes with the R31/R17 shell + task infrastructure.
//
// Both are R57+ scope: (i) duplicates the KPTI cr3 dance without
// benefit over (ii), and (ii) is the natural home for the exhaustive
// VFS-metadata coverage once a userspace `mkdir(1)` / `rmdir(1)` /
// `stat(1)` binary lands. Landing (ii) at R56.M3 would compose the
// syscall wire-up in the same round as the userspace client that
// exercises it, which conflates two independent verification tiers.
//
// The individual sys_*_body fingerprints are already witnessable
// through the ring-3 shell today (`sh: mkdir /tmp/d` etc. once
// userspace mkdir lands), and the R56.M3-002..005 per-body goldens
// cover each fingerprint's exact text. The R56.M3-006 composite
// smoke defers to that future userspace harness.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Composite fingerprint contract (for future R57 wire-up)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// tests/r56/expected-r56-meta.txt lists the six fingerprints a
// full-composite run would emit, in call order:
//
//   sys mkdir ok [legacy: SYS MKDIR OK]         (via sys_mkdir_body,   sysno 79)
//   sys stat ok [legacy: SYS STAT OK]           (via sys_stat_body,    sysno 78)
//   sys getdents ok [legacy: SYS GETDENTS OK]   (via sys_getdents_body,sysno 81)
//   sys rmdir ok [legacy: SYS RMDIR OK]         (via sys_rmdir_body,   sysno 80)
//   sys unlink ok [legacy: SYS UNLINK OK]       (via sys_unlink_body,  sysno 77)
//   sys rename ok [legacy: SYS RENAME OK]       (via sys_rename_body,  sysno 82)
//
// Each fingerprint is emitted by its own body's klog_s1_x1 tail on
// the success path; the witness (once wired) never emits its own
// per-primitive fingerprint. The five-line ordered subsequence
// mirrors the operational script this witness models:
//
//   mkdir /tmp/d      -> sys mkdir ok
//   stat  /tmp/d      -> sys stat ok
//   getdents /tmp     -> sys getdents ok
//   rmdir /tmp/d      -> sys rmdir ok
//   unlink /tmp/x     -> sys unlink ok  (x created via O_CREAT prior)
//   rename /tmp/a b   -> sys rename ok  (a created via O_CREAT prior)
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Wire posture at R56.M3
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// NOT wired into kernel_main / r30_platform. Symbol existence +
// build-time link verification are the R56.M3 acceptance criterion,
// matching the R54.M1-002 r54_bdev_flush.pdx and R55.M2-005
// r55_write_e2e.pdx precedents. Run-smoke mode `boot_r56_meta` is
// a SKIP-echo — the golden at tests/r56/expected-r56-meta.txt names
// the six ordered substrings a future FINGERPRINT_MODE flip would
// consume.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Reserved-label discipline
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Labels prefixed `r56m_` throughout. Grep audit: no `r56m_` hits
// anywhere else in src/kernel/ or tests/. Distinct from the
// per-body prefixes (sysmk_ mkdir, sysrm_ rmdir, sysstat_ stat,
// sysgd_ getdents, sysun_ unlink, sysrn_ rename).

module R56Meta = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // r56_meta_witness() -> u64
  //
  //   Returns 77 (SKIP sentinel) at R56.M3-006. The body is a
  //   scaffold — it does not touch any sys_*_body. See module
  //   header §"Why the body is deferred" for the aspace reason.
  //
  //   Alignment: entry rsp%16==8 (SysV, called from a leaf `call`
  //   site). One push (rbp) lands rsp%16==0 (aligned for any
  //   future nested call added at R57 wire-up). Matching pop
  //   restores rbp for the caller.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let r56_meta_witness : () -> u64 !{sysreg, mem} @{boot} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: { sysreg, mem },
      capabilities: { boot },
      justification: "R56.M3-006 (#1795). Dormant composite-smoke scaffold for the VFS-metadata syscall block (mkdir/rmdir/stat/getdents/unlink/rename, sysnos 77..82) landed by R56.M3-002..005 (#1791..#1794). Symbol-existence witness: links into build/kernel.elf and returns 77 (SKIP sentinel) without invoking any sys_*_body. Real invocation is deferred to R57 when a ring-3 harness (userspace mkdir(1)/stat(1)/rmdir(1)/... binaries) can exercise the six sysnos through the syscall trap — kernel-side calls into sys_*_body fail on `user_read_str_via_walk` against .bss scratch (walker resolves the caller-supplied path VA against the current task's page tables, so a kernel-only address either misses the mapping -> EFAULT or faults on a kernel page). The alternative — forging a synthetic user aspace around the call sequence — duplicates the KPTI cr3 dance without benefit over the ring-3 harness path. Body: 1-push (rbp) callee-save prologue lands rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8 + 8 = %16==0), aligned for the nested calls a future R57 wire-up will add. Immediate `mov rax, 77; pop rbp; ret`. Matches r54_bdev_flush_witness / r55_write_e2e_witness dormant-scaffold precedent. Composite fingerprint contract at tests/r56/expected-r56-meta.txt (six ordered substrings, one per sysno, matching each sys_*_body's own klog_s1_x1 tail emit). Reserved labels: r56m_.",
      block: {
        push rbp;
        mov rax, 77;
        pop rbp;
        ret
      }
    }
}
